# =============================================================================
# Convex first-time setup (fixes “no deployments” in the dashboard)
# =============================================================================
# Run these in YOUR machine’s terminal (interactive — browser login required):
#
#   1) npm run convex:login
#      Complete login in the browser (or paste the token when prompted).
#
#   2) npm run convex:dev
#      Pick “create a new project” or link an existing one. Leave this running
#      while you work — it pushes functions and writes deployment env vars.
#
#   After step 2, Convex creates/updates `.env.local` with `CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT`
#   and usually `VITE_CONVEX_URL`. Open the dashboard: npm run convex:dashboard
#
#   3) Edit `.env.local` and add this line if it is not there:
#        VITE_DATA_BACKEND=convex
#
#   4) In another terminal: npm run dev
#      Open Job List or Page Manager to trigger seed + data.
#
# =============================================================================
# Production / Vercel / Netlify (fixes “deployment” / empty Convex at runtime)
# =============================================================================
# Hosting cannot read `.env.local` (it is gitignored). You must configure env vars
# in the hosting UI **and** use a deploy key so `convex deploy` can run in CI.
#
# 1) Convex dashboard → your project → Production deployment → Settings →
#    General → “Generate Production Deploy Key” → copy `CONVEX_DEPLOY_KEY`
#
# 2) In Vercel: Project → Settings → Environment Variables
#    - CONVEX_DEPLOY_KEY = <paste>   (Production only is enough for prod deploys)
#    - VITE_DATA_BACKEND = convex    (Production — required so the app uses Convex)
#
# 3) Build command is set in `vercel.json` to:
#    npx convex deploy --cmd "npm run build" --cmd-url-env-var-name VITE_CONVEX_URL
#    That deploys functions, runs Vite with `VITE_CONVEX_URL` set for the bundle.
#
# 4) Local one-shot production build (after `npx convex dev` has configured the repo):
#    npm run deploy
#
# Preview deployments: use a Preview deploy key and Convex preview docs instead.
#
# =============================================================================
# Manual overrides (optional)
# =============================================================================
# Local mock API (default): omit VITE_DATA_BACKEND or set to anything except convex
# VITE_DATA_BACKEND=mock

# Use Convex for jobs, templates, assignment, and search/filtering:
# VITE_DATA_BACKEND=convex
# VITE_CONVEX_URL=https://YOUR-DEPLOYMENT.convex.cloud
